   "subject": "Comparison between LD-Matrix in \"mirt\" and in IRT PRO",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Phil and everyone,<div><br></div><div>I have been trying to do the same analysis in <a href=\"http://www.ssicentral.com/irt/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.ssicentral.com/irt/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473578688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0A0OTF22S4zisTD0JjD9S2\">IRT PRO</a> and with &quot;mirt&quot; packages in R. </div><div><br></div><div>In IRT PRO, it is suggested that LD &gt; 10 would be a suspect of local dependence; while I am wondering what would be the cut-off value in R? </div><div>I used the same <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473578688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0KYwmtJKemMIWaBCdj5RP5\">mirt packege codes updated on March 2018, page 134</a>. </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">residuals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> suppress </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br></div><div>I am wondering if <font color=\"#ff0000\">suppress=.15</font> here is a recommended threshold? Is there any reference or rationale that I could track down?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance,</div><div>Yingyi</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
