   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">The value is a correlation, which I think has a better overall interpretation than the cut-off of LD &gt; 10 setup (where exactly did that come from anyway?). Standardized correlation residuals have a common lineage with traditional factor analysis, though the actual magnitude may have different meaning. <div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Mar 28, 2018 at 3:39 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yingyi....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Phil and everyone,<div><br></div><div>I have been trying to do the same analysis in <a href=\"http://www.ssicentral.com/irt/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.ssicentral.com/irt/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473578688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0A0OTF22S4zisTD0JjD9S2\">IRT PRO</a> and with &quot;mirt&quot; packages in R. </div><div><br></div><div>In IRT PRO, it is suggested that LD &gt; 10 would be a suspect of local dependence; while I am wondering what would be the cut-off value in R? </div><div>I used the same <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/mirt/mirt.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473578688000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0KYwmtJKemMIWaBCdj5RP5\">mirt packege codes updated on March 2018, page 134</a>. </div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">residuals</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> suppress </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br><br></div><div>I am wondering if <font color=\"#ff0000\">suppress=.15</font> here is a recommended threshold? Is there any reference or rationale that I could track down?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance,</div><div>Yingyi</div></div></blockquote></div></div></div>"
