    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Who knows, I don&#39;t use IRTPRO so I&#39;m not sure what exactly it reports/does. I just followed the Chen and Thissen article, and applied my own correlation statistic based on standardizing tables. </div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Mar 28, 2018 at 3:40 PM,  <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">yingyi....@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">The LS matrix tables are different (in terms of the numbers) than the mirt package in R, though I am using the same analysis. </div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
